  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"line-height: 1.6em; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 200; color: #fafafa;\">🚀 <strong>Frontend</strong> Focus</td></tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #fafafa;\"><p>#​765 — November 4, 2026 | <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192441/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #fafafa; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the web</a></p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192398/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793796147/eduaw5bendeycfhsuy0l.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192398/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"webkit.org\">Safari Introduces Adaptive Dark Mode</a></span> — A new (opt-in) feature added to the Safari 27.3 beta that <em>automatically</em> adapts light sites to dark ones. It's here because although around 40% of pages are loaded by users using dark mode, only 10% of page loads directly support it.</p>\n<p>WebKit </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192397/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/b8bf63b6.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192397/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.meticulous.ai\">Agents Didn’t Clear Your Plate. They Dumped Reviews on It</a></span> — Your agents write PRs in minutes, then eat your afternoon in review. When did ‘saving time’ start to mean babysitting agents’ work? Meticulous verifies every UI change, with no developer effort. Devs at Dropbox &amp; ElevenLabs have their afternoons back. You can too.</p>\n<p>Meticulous <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192399/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.smashingmagazine.com\">Modern CSS Might Make Your Front-End More Complex</a></span> — Swapping JavaScript for container queries and <code>:has()</code> can cut your code down but introduce bugs elsewhere in your layout. Gabriel shares four examples, including why <code>container-type</code> can collapse flex items to zero width.</p>\n<p>Gabriel Shoyombo </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>📊</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192400/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"denodell.com\">Design Systems Should Be Fast by Default</a></span> — Den benchmarks dropdowns and checkbox lists across ten popular design systems, diagnoses the slowdowns, and shares tests to catch regressions.</p>\n<p>Den Odell </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">⚡️</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;\">IN BRIEF</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>🤚 The CSSWG <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192405/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">has resolved</a> that form controls get <code>cursor: pointer</code> by default under <code>appearance: base</code>. Cory LaViska explains the data and the objections.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🌐 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192401/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome 158 is in beta</a> (<em>stable due November 17</em>) with the &lt;<code>install</code>&gt; element, media pseudo-classes like <code>:playing</code> and <code>:paused</code>, <code>::highlight(*)</code>, and <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192442/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">XSLT is on its way out</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🆕 Rachel Andrew shares <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192402/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">an update on changes to the web platform</a> in October, including scroll-driven animations gaining support across all major engines.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🧰 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192403/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome DevTools has added</a> a visual position-area editor in Elements, Web Install manifest diagnostics, and MCP server improvements.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🤖 Google <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192404/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">will support a shared AI training control</a> in <code>robots.txt</code>, based on IETF AIPREF work, letting sites set a preference once for multiple AI providers.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">📙</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">Articles, Opinions &amp; Tutorials</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192406/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793797217/cw26e17ihpdwpaqhkxag.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192406/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"piccalil.li\">Native Masonry Layouts with CSS Grid Lanes</a></span> — A practical guide to native masonry layouts with CSS Grid Lanes, covering placement, fit-tolerance, horizontal layouts, subgrid and source-order accessibility. It's supported in only Safari right now, but other engines are working on it.</p>\n<p>Saleh Mubashar </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192407/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"rachelandrew.co.uk\">Making Features Generic in CSS</a></span> — Rachel takes a look at the new <code>flow-start</code> and <code>flow-end</code> alignment keywords, and touches upon why the CSSWG often renames things.</p>\n<p>Rachel Andrew </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192408/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"craftforms.app\">Embeddable Forms With Bookings, Live Pricing, and Payments Built In</a></span> — Build it visually, paste two lines into any site. Unlimited submissions on every plan with spam protection. From €6/mo.</p>\n<p>CraftForms <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192409/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"vale.rocks\">Quirks and Vintage Uses of CSS Table Display</a></span> — Looks back at <code>display: table</code> and its related values, sharing what each does and the pre-flexbox tricks they enabled — while of course noting that you probably shouldn't reach for them today. A neat history lesson.</p>\n<p>Declan Chidlow </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>🧡</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192410/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.mistys-internet.website\">If You Love a Website, Back It Up</a></span> — Following one of their favorite websites disappearing, a web-archiving practitioner explains how to go about preserving sites for yourself. A practical tour of browser-based capture techniques, automated crawling, and embedding the results.</p>\n<p>Misty De Meo </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192411/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793798261/pdysphxg4hnrkojir9jv.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192411/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"mofu-dev.com\">Spreading Liquid with Three.js</a></span> — A technical walkthrough of a neat liquid-spreading effect (built for a cosmetics campaign). It shows off using a height map for thickness, a velocity map for movement, and fragment shaders to render the result. There's a satisfying demo to play with, too.</p>\n<p>MISAKI NAKANO </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192412/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.ivankristianto.com\">How a Split Webfont Slowed Down Text Layout</a></span> — A font splitter put <code>i</code> and <code>j</code> in a different file from the rest of the alphabet, forcing extra text-shaping work within words (causing INP to suffer). Here's why, plus a script to check your own font CSS.</p>\n<p>Ivan Kristianto </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192413/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.tigerdata.com\">Why Is the Analytics Tab the Slowest Page in Your App?</a></span> — Usually it's one query scanning months of rows. TimescaleDB extends Postgres to make it fast. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192413/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Get $1000 credit</a>.</p>\n<p>Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192414/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.master.dev\">Multi-Column Different-Speed Scrolling</a></span> — There are some fun scrolling experiments here thanks to scroll-driven animations.</p>\n<p>Chris Coyier </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192415/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Useful <code>@custom-media</code> Presets</a></span>\n<br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Daniel Schwarz</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">⚠️</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;\">Third-Party Scripts</span></p>\n<p>Last week we <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192416/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">shared a PSA about forgotten script tags</a> and how what they load can be hijacked. Days later, a similar attack prominently appeared in the wild.</p>\n<p>On October 29, <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192417/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">a performance monitoring script on Polymarket was swapped for a wallet drainer</a>. The URL of the script didn't change, just the payload, so the CSP let it through, but Scott Helme's write-up explains what would have stopped it.</p>\n<p>Whatever you load from third parties, it's worth auditing for security, privacy, <em>and</em> performance reasons. Some steps worth taking:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pin scripts with <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192418/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Subresource Integrity</a> where the vendor's file is static, and use the new <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192419/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>Integrity-Policy-Report-Only</code> header</a> to find any you've missed.</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192420/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Self-host third-party resources</a> where you can. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192421/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Request Metrics explains</a> how it protects its own agent and why it's safe to self-host.</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192422/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Load third-party JavaScript efficiently</a>, or use <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192423/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Partytown</a> to move it off the main thread entirely.</li>\n<li>Audit what your page is loading with <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192424/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Request Map</a> and <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192425/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Third Party Web</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Lastly, if <em>you</em> provide third-party scripts to users, check out Jack Ellis's <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192443/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">writeup of how Fathom Analytics keeps their analytics script secure</a> for some tips.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">🧰</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">Tools, Code &amp; Resources</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192426/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/bftm7xl9zsrx0bcz8dcy.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192426/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"sidebearing-trim.js.org\">sidebearing-trim: Align Text by 'Visible Ink', Not by Glyph Boxes</a></span> — You can try it out interactively on the page and there's <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192427/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">a write-up of why you should care here</a>. One of those things that designers, in particular, are likely to notice! 😅 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192428/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo</a>.</p>\n<p>Pekka Lammi </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>🎨</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192429/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"colorsym.com\">ColorSym: Symbols to Identify Colors 'When Color Alone Isn't Enough'</a></span> — A way to use symbols to supplement colors, aiding with accessibility. The symbols are 'intelligent' where, for example, the orange symbol is a combo of those for red and yellow. Available as SVGs or a custom font.</p>\n<p>Chris Eastridge &amp; Luis Francisco </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192430/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"astrotypes.com\">Astrotypes: Curated Font Pairings for Astro</a></span> — Search and preview font pairings sourced from Google Fonts, Bunny CDN, and Fontshare live on the page. Each pair has a copy command for various tools (npm, Yarn, Bun, etc).</p>\n<p>Michael Andreuzza </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192431/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">File Viewer: A Browser-Native Office, PDF, CAD, and Archive Viewer for Internal Web Apps</a></span> — Provides read-only views for Office, PDF/OFD, CAD, archives, email and more, with integrations for React, Vue, and Svelte. There's also <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192444/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">a live demo</a> to try.</p>\n<p>Flyfish Dev </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>Know React? Then you and your coding agent can ship iOS and Android apps. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192433/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo</a> runs the builds and CI/CD and gets you into the app stores.</p>\n<p>🧪 In-browser testing inside your dev server. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192434/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">TWD</a> adds a test sidebar next to your app, and your AI agent runs it too. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192434/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Free and MIT</a>.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">🔤</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">...and finally</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192435/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/yk9k2ocjsueook0r53oa.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192435/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"vercel.com\">Introducing Geist <em>Serif</em></a></span> — Vercel's Geist family gains a high-contrast display serif for headlines, built on the same metrics as Geist Sans so the two mix cleanly. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192436/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Geist Sans</a>, <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192437/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Geist Mono</a> and <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/192438/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Geist Pixel</a> are on Google Fonts already; Serif isn't yet, but will be in due course.</p>\n<p>Vercel </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
